   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let m(x) = ln(25 - x^2) / (x + 2). Consider the largest interval that contains x = 0 and on which m is continuous. What is the sum of the integers in that interval?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 9
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The logarithm requires 25 - x^2 > 0, so -5 < x < 5, and the denominator x + 2 is zero at x = -2, so that input is excluded as well.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Subtract",
            25,
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "m is a quotient of a logarithmic function and a polynomial, each continuous on its domain, so m is continuous on (-5, -2) U (-2, 5).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Ln",
               [
                  "Subtract",
                  25,
                  [
                     "Power",
                     "x",
                     2
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The piece that contains x = 0 is (-2, 5), open at -2 because of the denominator and open at 5 because ln 0 is undefined. Its integers are -1, 0, 1, 2, 3 and 4.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            -1,
            0,
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The sum of those integers is 9.",
         "mathjson": 9
      }
   ],
